# Gate step 1293-wka4 — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. run-litmus-test.sh runs under `set -uo pipefail`, but that is
# a property of THAT shell. Each step is spawned with a fresh `bash -c`, which
# does not inherit it — so `producer | head` returned 0 when the producer exited
# non-zero, and a step declaring `assert_exit: 0` adjudicated HEAD's status
# rather than the producer's. The row's reproduction returned 0 and now returns 7.
#
# THE DESIGN IS THE GATING, NOT THE PIPEFAIL. A blanket would have been one line
# and wrong. Measured on this corpus: 25 steps declaring assert_exit have a
# top-level pipe, but only 3 end in a status-swallowing consumer; the other 22
# end in `grep -q`, where grep IS the adjudicator, and several are NEGATED — for
# those, pipefail INVERTS the verdict (a failing producer today makes the
# pipeline 0 and the negation 1/fail; under pipefail it becomes non-zero and the
# negation 0/pass). So the prelude is applied only where the shape swallows a
# status AND the status actually decides the verdict (the step declares
# assert_exit, or declares no expectation at all and falls to the strict-exit
# arm). Shape alone matched 206 of 2553 steps; with the second condition it is
# 5, in 5 files. ARM 4b is the regression guard for the 22.
#
# THE TWO CONDITIONS ARE BOTH LOAD-BEARING and neither is obvious from the
# defect report, which is why they are written here rather than inferred later.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER, PINNED BY ARM 5 RATHER THAN OMITTED: a step whose
# command is `bash -lc '... | tee ...'` runs its pipeline in a GRANDCHILD, and
# the prelude set in the spawned shell does not reach it (measured: rc=0) — this
# row's own defect one level down. SHELLOPTS is the usual propagation route and
# is READONLY here, so that route is closed. ARM 5 ASSERTS THE HOLE, so if
# someone later closes it the arm FAILS and demands the limitation be
# re-recorded instead of quietly passing. Two of the three corpus steps in the
# hazard class have that shape, and both are on unbound-grandfathered.txt —
# they have never been run by any suite, so their exposure is latent and will
# arrive when 660-ryhn binds them.
#
# ARM 3 IS THE PRE-FIX CONTROL: it neutralises the prelude in a COPY of the
# runner and requires the false green to return, asserting the mutation LANDED
# (live >= 1 occurrence, mutant 0) before reading any verdict — a sed that
# matched nothing yields a copy identical to the subject, and "the defect did
# not reproduce" would then be indistinguishable from "the mutation never
# applied".
#
# VERIFIED BEYOND THE FIXTURE: the two reachable corpus tests whose steps now
# carry the prelude were executed and PASS (litmus:plan-engine-invariants-shape,
# litmus:podman-idiomatic-error-discrimination). The third is phase 4 / e2e and
# needs a GUI terminal; the remaining two are the orphans named above.
#
# COST, MEASURED HERE 2026-09-20: 0.37 / 0.37 s. It runs the real runner against
# a throwaway corpus in a temp dir — no compile, no container, no network, and
# it never writes into openspec/litmus-tests.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose: a binding assembled from a variable
# is invisible to every name-based scan, including the bound-or-retired guard
# (1063-nraf). Keep it a plain string.
STEP_DESC="Checking a step's producer failing into a filter reaches the verdict (1293-wka4)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-litmus-step-pipefail.sh"
STEP_ERROR="a litmus step's producer can again fail into head/tee/wc and be reported green, or the pipefail gating has widened into a blanket that inverts grep-adjudicated steps (1293-wka4) — read which arm failed above; ARM 4b failing means the blanket was applied, ARM 3 failing means the fixture can no longer reproduce the defect"
STEP_OK="A step's producer failure reaches its verdict"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:litmus-step-pipefail:6/6"
